## 2. Design rationale

### Four short steps, one persistent summary

Separate steps preserve the requested order and reduce competing choices at 375 px. Wellness and vaccination appear first; **Any available vet** is preselected to remove an unnecessary decision. Native radio groups support touch, keyboard and screen readers.

The summary updates immediately. Changing service resets vet preference and time; changing vet resets time. Editing without changing a selection preserves it. With “Any,” selecting a slot reveals its specific vet before confirmation.

The layout uses flexible widths, wrapping text, 16 px page gutters and no fixed-height panels or sticky overlays. Controls have at least 48 px-high interactive areas; focus is visible, step changes focus the heading, and summary changes are announced.

### “From” pricing

“From $280” remains explicitly a starting price—not a promised total. The supplied data cannot support a no-surprises dental booking. Production needs an exact clinic quote accepted before confirmation; until then, confirmation is blocked. This dataset has no valid dental slot anyway.

### Brand departure

White on `#7FD1AE` has approximately **1.8:1** contrast, below WCAG AA even for large text. Primary buttons retain mint backgrounds but use `#1D2B33` labels, approximately **8:1** contrast. Dark borders also identify button boundaries against white.

Other supplied tokens are retained. This implements key AA requirements, but production still needs keyboard, screen-reader, zoom/reflow and device testing.

## 3. Data problems and handling

| Problem | Handling |
|---|---|
| Richard: exotic check-up, 10:00 | Reject: only Mary is qualified. |
| Mary: dental cleaning, 11:30 | Reject: 90 minutes ends at 13:00 and overlaps lunch. |
| Richard: wellness, 12:30 | Reject: appointment begins during lunch. |
| Mary: wellness, 16:45 | Reject: appointment ends at 17:15, after closing. |
| Remaining valid records | Show **Mary’s exotic check-up, 11:00–11:45**, and **Richard’s wellness exam, 14:00–14:30**, only for matching selections. |
| No vaccination slots; no valid dental slots | Show an honest empty state. Do not manufacture availability from working hours or describe missing records as “fully booked.” |
| Thursday has no date or timezone | Clearly label the illustrative date. Production must return dated timestamps and the clinic’s timezone. |
| Dental has only a minimum price | Require an exact quote before committing; the API must provide the final payable total, including applicable mandatory charges. |
| Vet/service references are names; no slot IDs | Production should use stable vet, service and slot identifiers. Demo IDs are local only. |
| Availability may change after selection | Server must enforce qualifications, schedules, full-duration fit, price and inventory atomically. On conflict, retain choices, explain the issue and offer refreshed times—not a false confirmation. |

Both vets work Thursday; Mary’s Tue/Thu/Sat restriction must also be enforced when other dates are introduced.

